suggestions.sketch:
Create a new class in the application layer:

```python
class OrderReportService:
    def __init__(self, repo: OrderRepository, mailer: EmailClient):
        self._repo = repo
        self._mailer = mailer

    def count_orders(self) -> int:
        return self._repo.count()

    def send_summary(self, address: str) -> dict[str, str]:
        return self._mailer.send(address, f"{self._repo.count()} orders")
```
Then refactor ReportView to depend only on this service:

```python
class ReportView:
    def __init__(self, service: OrderReportService) -> None:
        self._service = service
        self._width = 40

    def title(self) -> str:
        return "Orders".center(self._width, "-")

    def describe_customer(self, customer) -> str:
        parts = [str(customer.customer_id()), customer.name(), customer.email(), customer.tier()]
        return " | ".join(parts).ljust(self._width)

    def order_count(self) -> int:
        return self._service.count_orders()

    def mail_summary(self, address: str) -> dict[str, str]:
        return self._service.send_summary(address)
```
This keeps ReportView focused on formatting, while the service handles data access and email logic, satisfying the presentation layer’s import constraints.

